what's up doc ready to jam  the sequel to space jam is finally here  with lebron james bugs bunny  and the rest of the looney tunes taking  center stage  space jam a new legacy wouldn't be the  pop culture bonanza it is without its  visual effects  to celebrate the release of this sequel  let's look at some of the magic that  went on behind the scenes  let's get some birds in these seats  space jam a new legacy is set in the  digital world known as  the server verse a virtual playground  filled with hundreds of characters from  the warner brothers library  ranging from icons like batman and  scooby-doo to even r-rated characters  like the white walkers from game of  thrones  and the droogs from a clockwork orange  in order to create this server-verse  setting the vfx team had to challenge  themselves and go to lengths they've  never gone before  the film's headliner lebron james has  gone on record to say just how impressed  he is with the film's effects  i think the effects that we have  throughout the film are going to be the  greatest thing about the whole movie  that's quite the promise to make for  lebron producer ryan coogler who is no  stranger to franchise films directing  films like black panther  and creed was equally impressed with the  work of the film's animation team  spice jam really takes advantage of all  the cutting-edge filmmaking technology  the film's flashy and glorious chaotic  style makes coogler's statement  very easy to believe especially when you  consider just how much innovation went  into the first film  visual effects supervisor grady cofer  stressed in an interview  just how much work was put into making  the film look as  visually appealing as possible it takes  hundreds and hundreds of artists  building shots it took the animators and  vfx artists quite some time to finish  some of the shots  a shot such as this one featuring the  countless warner brothers icons  like the flintstones and king kong  rushing down the lush  animated landscapes of the server verse  easily took almost  a year of hard work to complete that's a  pretty hefty workload to say the least  the sequence following lebron falling  through the server-verse required some  practical work as james flies past  planets themed to game of thrones the  maltese falcon  dc comics and the wizard of oz wires  were attached to lebron to make it seem  like he was actually falling through the  server verse instead of just  standing in front of a green screen  classic  a major noticeable difference between a  new legacy and its 1996 predecessor  is the new legacy's mix of 2d and 3d  animation compared to the 1996 film's  strictly 2d stylings in the vein of the  comedy classic  who framed roger rabbit in fact ed jones  the special effects supervisor behind  roger rabbit  also served on the crew of space jam  further linking the two  films as for a new legacy one of the  biggest obstacles the animators faced  was designing 3d models for the classic  looney tunes characters and giving them  a look and feel that wouldn't betray  their original design or make them feel  overly modernized i look expensive  the team also wanted to make sure that  the film didn't feel too artificial  and wanted to really make the animated  tunes look as good as they possibly  could  this meant adding new features to these  characters that had never been done  before  in a featurette the film's animation  production designer devin crane said  we have all these textures and layers  and artistic complexities we really  wanted to make it film as handcrafted as  possible  the cg artists also found themselves  having to come up with new ways to bring  the world of warner brothers to life  cg supervisor abzuromi has said while  that process was to develop some new  tools to achieve that 2d aspect in the  3d world  lebron also faced some challenges  regarding the film's animation-heavy  setting  lebron was primarily acting against a  green screen and interacting with  characters that weren't actually there  on set  behind the scenes shots show lebron  acting opposite cardboard cutouts of  looney tunes characters  along with a crowd of extras dressed as  iconic characters from the warner  brothers library  another area that was new to lebron that  even michael jordan didn't have to take  part in  was to also be portrayed as a fully  animated character  alongside his live-action appearances  this was likely done because of his  extremely busy schedule playing for the  lakers as the movie was filmed over the  course of two years complete with the  live  action filming as well as all the  animation work the global pandemic was  another obstacle that the team faced  when working on the movie  like many movies much of the film's vfx  was done in post-production  but due to the circumstances provided  the animators and visual effects artists  all had to work from home even the voice  actors from the likes of veterans like  jeff bergman who provides his voice to  bugs bunny to superstars like zendaya  who voices lola bunny  had to record their lines from their own  home  i feel quite lucky to play such an  iconic  character at least voice her so i feel  pretty lucky bergman has said that this  was one of the first times in his career  as a voice actor  that he didn't get to meet the other  voice actors while recording his lines  who wouldn't be bummed about not getting  their chance to work with zendaya  hopefully he'll get his chance in space  jam 3.  i'm a cartoon what's up dad  space jam a new legacy was made on a  massive budget  of over 150 million nearly doubling the  original film's budget of 80 million  with how much technology has changed  over the years this shouldn't be  too surprising as trailers for the films  seem to be promising a true  looney tunes blockbuster sequel a space  jam sequel has been in the works for  quite some time  going through several phases one with  jackie chan titled  spy jam another featuring jeff gordon  titled  race jam and even a golf-themed sequel  headlined by tiger woods with a  supporting turn by michael jordan  ultimately the studio went with the  brendan fraser-led looney tunes back in  action  which proved to be a financial  disappointment  at the time wb was also working on a  direct sequel to space jam starring tony  hawk  which was eventually cancelled after the  poor performance of back in action  it wasn't until 2016 when the studio  decided to move forward with an official  sequel to space jam  when they felt they had the proper  technology and concept to make a true  follow-up  a reality lebron was coming off a  successful supporting turn in the amy  schumer comedy train wreck and had  recently signed a deal between his  production company  spring hill and warner bros and thus  space jam a new legacy  became a reality motion capture was one  of the key components used to enact some  of the film's basketball-themed stunts  which couldn't be performed in any other  way in particular  scenes required lebron to be thrown on  alley-oop  which required the crew to place the  camera behind the basket  the film's director malcolm d lee talked  about some of the difficulties filming  the scene saying  so it was a very small window to get the  shot so lebron caught it kind of high  and really just  threw his arm back and threw it down and  i jumped out of my seat  and i loved it because i wasn't really  trying to motivate him but it was kind  of a happy accident  of course a space jam sequel wouldn't  really be a true basketball film if  lebron didn't get to show off his  basketball skills on screen  and from the looks of it he'll continue  to prove to fans around the world  why he's one of the greatest at what he  does  i gotta say i think this is gonna be one  of the coolest movies people are ever  gonna see  it's clear that the cast and crew behind  space jam a new legacy had some  obstacles to face when creating the  film's  cg heavy setting but thanks to their  innovation and commitment to the film  the looney tunes are looking better than  ever for their reinvention of the 1996  classic are you excited to see space jam  a new legacy
 

